#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/polkit.xml:92
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"duktape\"/> and <xref linkend=\"glib2\"/> (GObject "
"Introspection recommended)"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"duktape\"/> e <xref linkend=\"glib2\"/> (GObject "
"Introspection recomendado)"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/polkit.xml:96
#, xml-text
msgid "Recommended"
msgstr "Recomendadas"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/polkit.xml:98
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libxslt\"/>,<phrase revision=\"systemd\"> and</phrase> <xref"
" linkend=\"linux-pam\"/><phrase revision=\"sysv\">, and <xref "
"linkend=\"elogind\"/> </phrase>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"libxslt\"/>,<phrase revision=\"systemd\"> e</phrase> <xref "
"linkend=\"linux-pam\"/><phrase revision=\"sysv\"> e <xref "
"linkend=\"elogind\"/> </phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/polkit.xml:106
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Since <phrase revision=\"sysv\"><command>elogind</command></phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><command>systemd-logind</command></phrase> uses PAM to "
"register user sessions, it is a good idea to build "
"<application>Polkit</application> with PAM support so <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\"><command>elogind</command></phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><command>systemd-logind</command></phrase> can track "
"<application>Polkit</application> sessions."
msgstr ""
"Como <phrase revision=\"sysv\"><command>elogind</command></phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><command>systemd-logind</command></phrase> usa PAM para"
" registrar sessões de usuário(a), é uma boa ideia construir "
"<application>Polkit</application> com suporte a PAM, de forma que <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\"><command>elogind</command></phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><command> systemd-logind</command></phrase> possa "
"rastrear sessões <application>Polkit</application>."

